      "text": null,
      "title": "The Astronomical Clock, Prague 📌\n\nBuilt in 1410, this incredible medieval clock has been keeping time for more than 600 years. Its astronomical dial shows the position of the Sun and Moon, while every hour, the Twelve Apostles make their procession above the Old Town Square. Standing here feels like watching history tick by! \n\nA true masterpiece of medieval engineering, the clock stands within Prague’s UNESCO-listed Historic Centre, making this one of the city’s most iconic landmarks. Don’t miss it when visiting this incredible city.\n\nAstronomical clock, Prague 📍\n\n#astronomicalclockprague #praguehistoriccentre #unescowordheritage #travellingprague #exploreprague🇨🇿",
